From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:16:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: name the wakeup
 sources

Nothing on the station is marked as able to wake the system, so a
suspend could only end on an RTC alarm. Mark three:

- the power key (Esc), the vendor's own wake key;
- the keyboard matrix, so a key wakes the system while the lid is open;
  the keypad driver only arms it while the keyboard is enabled, and the
  lid policy disables the keyboard while the lid is closed;
- the hall switch, on deassertion only: opening the lid wakes the
  system, closing it does not.

The keyboard needs the AW9523 wake support in the previous patch. The
hall node stays disabled here; the station's DT composition enables it.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts  | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 98acc62f4..21dbe5120 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 
 #include "mt6797-gemini-pda-wifi-service.dts"
 #include <dt-bindings/iio/adc/mediatek,mt6351-auxadc.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/gpio-keys.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/thermal/thermal.h>
 
 / {
@@ -282,6 +283,16 @@ &aw9523 {
 &{/keyboard-matrix} {
 	/delete-property/ poll-interval;
 	held-poll-interval = <20>;
+	/* A key wakes the system while the lid is open (needs the AW9523 wake). */
+	wakeup-source;
+};
+
+/* Opening the lid wakes the system; closing it does not. */
+&hall_gpio_keys {
+	hall-switch {
+		wakeup-source;
+		wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_DEASSERTED>;
+	};
 };
 
 &thermal {
@@ -300,6 +311,7 @@ keys {
 		/* The driver assigns the PMIC keys by child order: power, then home. */
 		power-key {
 			linux,keycodes = <KEY_ESC>;
+			wakeup-source;
 		};
 
 		home-key {
